coutu@cithe303.cithep.caltech.edu (Stephane Coutu) writes:
> Why don't those of you out there who have some inkling of what's to come
> post a few hints about what we can expect?

The dungeon should look more interesting.  Lines of sight and light
sources will affect what you can see, and there may be an option to
display the lit part of a corridor in a different character.  The dull
old hell and endgame levels should have some interesting new
geography, too.

There could be subquests, which may differ for some character classes,
for items you will need to get the Amulet of Yendor, which may lead you
into separate branches of the dungeon where new special levels await.

Of course, some of our favorite bugs will be fixed, like the infamous
negative-weight bag of holding bug.  Some old tricks won't work (like
a certain trick to generate spell books), and others may have new
risks or side effects.

There will probably not be superheroes, phone booths, revolving doors,
soccer stadiums, radioactive chickens, RoboCops or ED-209s.  There
probably won't be a shopping mall, but there may be a level with two
or three shops.  There may not be loads of new items or hordes of new
monsters (though there will be a few), but some familiar things may be
better integrated into the game.

So NetHack 3.1 will be very different, and it will be very the same.
Expect to be surprised (until the spoilers catch up :-).


